        "original_id": "ab16824b-c3b1-525f-a3f2-7b3573a0748f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joel Chandler Harris, James Baskett\n- Works: Song of the South, Uncle Remus stories\n- Characters: Uncle Remus, Br'er Rabbit\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company\n\nFacts:\n- Joel Chandler Harris adapted the Uncle Remus stories.\n- In 1946, The Walt Disney Company adapted Br'er Rabbit for the animated motion picture Song of the South.\n- In 1946, Song of the South was based on the collection of Uncle Remus stories as adapted by Joel Chandler Harris.\n- In 1946, James Baskett starred as Uncle Remus in the Disney feature film Song of the South.\n- In 1946, James Baskett sang the song \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah\" in Song of the South.\n- James Baskett was born on February 16, 1904, and died on July 9, 1948.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
