        "text": "Page: Song of the South. Sentence: It is based on the collection of Uncle Remus stories as adapted by Joel Chandler Harris, and stars James Baskett as Uncle Remus.\nPage: James Baskett. Sentence: James Baskett (February 16, 1904 – July 9, 1948) was an American actor known for his portrayal of Uncle Remus, singing the song \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah\" in the 1946 Disney feature film \"Song of the South\".\nPage: Br'er Rabbit. Sentence: The Walt Disney Company later adapted this character for its 1946 animated motion picture \"Song of the South\".",
